# bb-contents Core Conventions

Project identity, stack, and release mapping live in **`PROJECT.md`** at the repo
root. Generic engineering standards live in the other `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`. This
file holds the **bb-contents-specific** coding contract.

## Architecture

`@bebranded/bb-contents` is a zero-dependency vanilla-JS library for Webflow,
activated by `bb-*` / `data-bb-*` HTML attributes.

- **Source of truth is `src/`.** `src/core.js` is the bundle entry (config, init,
  helpers, `MutationObserver`, `utils`, `attrMap`). Each feature is one ES module
  in `src/modules/<name>.js` with a `export default` object.
- **`bb-contents.js`, `bb-contents.min.js`, `bb-contents.min.js.map` are GENERATED**
  by esbuild (`build.js`). Never edit them by hand — edit `src/` and run
  `npm run build`.
- esbuild bundles everything into a single self-executing IIFE that sets
  `window.bbContents`. No external runtime dependency may ever be added.

## Module Contract

Every module is an ES module exporting a single object with an `init(scope)`:

```js
/**
 * Module ModuleName
 * One-line French description of what it does.
 *
 * @attr {string} bb-name - Enables the module on the element
 * @attr {'a'|'b'} [bb-name-option=a] - Option description
 */
export default {
    init(scope) {
        // 1. Respect the global disable switch
        if (scope.closest && scope.closest('[data-bb-disable]')) return;

        // 2. Query with _attrSelector (dual bb-* / data-bb-* support)
        const elements = scope.querySelectorAll(bbContents._attrSelector('name'));

        elements.forEach(function (element) {
            // 3. Idempotency guard — re-init on the same element is a no-op
            if (element.hasAttribute('data-bb-name-processed')) return;
            element.setAttribute('data-bb-name-processed', '1');

            // 4. Read options via _getAttr; sanitize before any DOM insertion
            const opt = bbContents._getAttr(element, 'bb-name-option') || 'a';

            // ... module logic ...
        });

        bbContents.utils.log('Module ModuleName initialisé:', elements.length, 'éléments');
    }
};
```

Rules:
- **Always query with `bbContents._attrSelector('name')`** — it accepts the bare
  name (`'current-year'`) or the prefixed form (`'bb-current-year'`) and emits the
  dual `[bb-name], [data-bb-name]` selector.
- **Always read values with `bbContents._getAttr(element, 'bb-name-option')`.**
- **Always guard idempotency** with the `data-bb-name-processed` attribute (some
  older modules also set `element.bbProcessed` — either works, but be consistent
  within a module). The `MutationObserver` re-calls `init()` on new nodes, so a
  guard is mandatory.
- **Always honor `[data-bb-disable]`** at the top of `init`.

### Registering a module in `core.js`

A new module is not active until it is wired into `src/core.js` in **all** of:
1. `import name from './modules/name.js';`
2. the `modules: { ... }` object
3. the `attrMap` (maps the trigger attribute → module key, e.g.
   `'country-select': 'countrySelect'`) — this is the single source of truth for
   detection; there is no per-module `detect` function anymore
4. `_optionRules` (one entry per option attribute, for dev-mode validation)

## Security

Before any DOM insertion (helpers live in `bbContents.utils`):
- Text content → `bbContents.utils.sanitize(value)`
- CSS values → `bbContents.utils.escapeCss(value)`
- URLs → validate with `bbContents.utils.isValidUrl(url)` first
- Country codes → validate with `bbContents.utils.isValidCountryCode(code)`

See the generic `security.mdc` for the broader baseline. The YouTube API key is
**never** in the browser — it lives only in the Cloudflare Worker
(`youtube-worker.js`); the module fetches `window._bbContentsConfig.youtubeEndpoint`.

## Error Handling

Never leave an empty or silent `catch`. At minimum log through the project logger:

```js
} catch (e) {
    console.error('[bb-contents] Module failed:', e);
}
```

Retry loops must have a hard max — never poll infinitely without a timeout.

## Documentation

**Every code change must be reflected in documentation** (see `github-workflow.mdc`).

- **JSDoc** above each module: purpose + every supported `@attr`.
- **`README.md`**: public reference — add/update a section and the attribute table
  on any new module or attribute change.
- **`docs/<module>.md`**: per-module detailed doc — keep in sync.

| Action | JSDoc | README + docs/ |
|---|---|---|
| Add a module | Required | Required |
| Add an attribute | Required | Required |
| Change behavior | Update | Update if user-facing |
| Bug fix (no API change) | — | — |

## Publishing Workflow

**The version must be identical in 2 source places; the generated banner follows
automatically:**
1. `package.json` → `"version"`
2. `src/core.js` → `const BB_CONTENTS_VERSION = '...'`
3. `bb-contents.js` → `@version` banner — **generated** by `build.js` from
   `package.json`; do not edit by hand. Run `npm run build` after a bump.

| Target | GitHub | npm |
|---|---|---|
| `develop` / test | `git push origin develop` | `npm publish --tag test` |
| `main` / live | `git push origin main` | `npm publish` (tag `latest`) |

Always rebuild (`npm run build`) and commit the regenerated bundles with the
version bump. See the `bump-and-publish` skill for the full checklist.
